# This package verifies several files by sha256, so their bytes must survive a
# clone exactly. `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout and silently breaks every recorded digest: a fresh clone reported
# `deck-framework.md size drifted: 32185 != recorded 31630` because 555 lines had
# been converted. These rules make the working tree byte-identical everywhere.

# Verified payload: sha256-recorded in assets/frames/SOURCES.json.
assets/frames/** -text

# Generated patch: compared line-for-line against the preset package's patch.
cordis.patch.yml -text

# Plugin sources: shell scripts and Node ESM are line-ending agnostic, but keeping
# them LF keeps diffs and the verbatim patch comparison honest.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
